# Private planning material — never commit
.private/
CLAUDE.md

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Staged artefacts: fetched by `make stage`, never committed
models/
bundle/
dist/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/

# Editor config (local only)
.vscode/

# Local Claude worktrees are separate Git checkouts.
/.claude/worktrees/

# Local review screenshots, produced by UI review sessions. Never part of the
# submission; kept out so `git add -A` cannot ship one.
review-*.png

# Internal review write-ups. These belong in .private/ (HANDOFF §3.12); ignored
# at the repo root as a backstop so `git add -A` cannot ship one into the
# submission. Narrow paths, so a deliberate doc is never caught by accident.
# Anchored AND unanchored on purpose. Both files cite .private/ paths by name,
# and a copy of either under docs/ walked past the anchored form -- which matters
# more here than it looks, because scripts/package-offline.sh seals the bundle
# with `git archive HEAD`, so anything committed once ships in every bundle after.
/DEVOPS_REVIEW.md
/REVIEW_PLAN.md
DEVOPS_REVIEW.md
REVIEW_PLAN.md

# The dress-rehearsal prompts and their report, same block and same reason. They
# were untracked and stageable until 2026-09-28, when they moved to .private/;
# `git check-ignore` matched none of them, so nothing but care stopped a
# `git add -A` from committing them -- and `git archive HEAD` would then have
# shipped an internal hiring-review corpus in every bundle after. Anchored and
# unanchored, because the report sat under docs/ and the prompts at the root.
# No rule for docs/rehearsal-review/ on purpose. Until this commit two files
# under it were tracked, and .gitignore does not untrack anything, so a pattern
# there would have shadowed a tracked path -- a trap rather than a backstop. Both
# moved to .private/ here, so the directory is now empty of tracked files; the
# rule is still not worth adding, because the only way one appears under it again
# is somebody deciding to put it there.
/HIRING_MANAGER_DRESS_REHEARSAL_PROMPT.md
/HIRING_MANAGER_NEXT_OPUS_BATCH.md
HIRING_MANAGER_DRESS_REHEARSAL_PROMPT.md
HIRING_MANAGER_NEXT_OPUS_BATCH.md
HIRING_MANAGER_DRESS_REHEARSAL_REPORT.md

# Operational backups (scripts/backup-state.sh, demos/06_backup_restore.sh).
# Real database and outbox contents, written beside the stack. Never committed.
backups/

# Event re-check evidence ledgers (scripts/event-recheck.sh). An append-only
# record of what each venue page said when it was last opened, written beside
# the stack by the operator who ran the probe. It is local operational
# evidence, not part of the submission.
.recheck/
